# qkt Bybit project

This project was generated by `qkt create template --kind bybit`.

It starts a qkt daemon and the [qkt-venue-gateway](https://github.com/elitekaycy/qkt-venue-gateway)
running its Bybit adapter. qkt trades Bybit only through the gateway (a `type: gateway` broker),
the same way it trades every other gateway venue. Testnet is the starting point.

Read `CONFIG.md` for a plain-English explanation of `.env`, `docker-compose.yml`,
`qkt.config.yaml`, Bybit credentials, alerts, and state. The adapter's own page lists its
settings and venue behaviour:
https://github.com/elitekaycy/qkt-venue-gateway/blob/main/adapter-bybit/README.md

## First Run

```bash
cp .env.example .env
$EDITOR .env
docker compose --env-file .env config --quiet
make up
make gateway-health
make status
```

`make gateway-health` should show `"adapter":"bybit"`, your account as `account_login`
(copy it into `BYBIT_ACCOUNT_LOGIN` if you left it blank, then `make restart`) and
`"venue_connected":true`.

## Environment Values

Start with Bybit testnet:

```dotenv
QKT_IMAGE_TAG=v{{QKT_VERSION}}
BYBIT_TRADER_TOKEN=          # any long random string
BYBIT_GUARDIAN_TOKEN=        # another one
BYBIT_API_KEY=
BYBIT_API_SECRET=
BYBIT_ENVIRONMENT=testnet
BYBIT_TRADE_MODE=demo
BYBIT_ACCOUNT_LOGIN=
```

Optional Telegram alerts:

```dotenv
TELEGRAM_ENABLED=false
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
```

Set `BYBIT_ENVIRONMENT=mainnet` and `BYBIT_TRADE_MODE=real` only after you have validated
the strategy and intend to trade real Bybit funds. qkt refuses to start if the gateway's
trade mode and `BYBIT_TRADE_MODE` disagree.

Keep `.env` out of Git.

## Commands

Use these commands from the project directory:

```bash
make up                         # start the Bybit gateway and the qkt daemon
make logs                       # tail daemon logs
make gateway-logs               # tail gateway logs
make gateway-health             # the gateway's adapter, account and venue connection
make status                     # show deployed strategies
make deploy STRAT=ema_cross     # deploy strategies/ema_cross.qkt
make resync-dry-run STRAT=ema_cross
make resync STRAT=ema_cross
make reconcile STRAT=ema_cross
make stop STRAT=ema_cross
make down                       # stop containers without deleting state
```

## Strategy Flow

1. Use testnet credentials first.
2. Review and backtest the strategy outside this deployment repo
   (`qkt fetch BYBIT_LINEAR:BTCUSDT --tf 5m --last 30d` reads bars through the gateway).
3. Copy the live-ready `.qkt` file into `strategies/`.
4. Deploy with `make deploy STRAT=<name>`.
5. For edits, run `make resync-dry-run`, then `make resync`, then `make reconcile`.

